ComplexType"></FIELD><FIELD Name="OTFT Article"></FIELD><FIELD Name="IsComposite"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Sensitivity"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Retention Policy"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Created By">claude-code</FIELD><FIELD Name="Created On">20260828 090738.259</FIELD><FIELD Name="Updated By"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Updated On"></FIELD></ROW><ROW><FIELD Name="OTFT Name">Pick Up Date</FIELD><FIELD Name="Alias"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Type">L</FIELD><FIELD Name="Derivable?"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Subtype?">F</FIELD><FIELD Name="Data Type">date</FIELD><FIELD Name="Length"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Scale"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Reducable?"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Reduce!"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Comment"></FIELD><FIELD Name="SyncLink">01A04732-1242-7C5E-A0FA-734F0B661613</FIELD><FIELD Name="Artificial Key"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Estimated number of Tuples"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Static population"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Namespace"></FIELD><FIELD Name="NamespaceVersion"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Is super type"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Is abstract type"></FIELD><FIELD Name="OTFT Schema"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Abbreviation"></FIELD><FIELD Name="OTFT Plural"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Temporal"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Transitional"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Concept Type"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Task Status"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Task Color"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Task Background"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Localize Value"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Image URI"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Meta Level">1</FIELD><FIELD Name="Authoritative Synclink">01A04732-1242-7D75-85BA-5840A86C0E22</FIELD><FIELD Name="Case Sensitive"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Annotatable"></FIELD><FIELD Name="IsComplexType"></FIELD><FIELD Name="OTFT Article"></FIELD><FIELD Name="IsComposite"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Sensitivity"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Retention Policy"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Created By">claude-code</FIELD><FIELD Name="Created On">20260828 090738.946</FIELD><FIELD Name="Updated By"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Updated On"></FIELD></ROW><ROW><FIELD Name="OTFT Name">R01 Car Model Belongs To One Car Group</FIELD><FIELD Name="Alias"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Type">R</FIELD><FIELD Name="Derivable?">F</FIELD><FIELD Name="Subtype?">F</FIELD><FIELD Name="Data Type"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Length"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Scale"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Reducable?"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Reduce!"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Comment">[Definition]
It is necessary that each car model is classified in exactly one car group. Enforced structurally: UC on role 1 of "Car Group of Car Model" plus TC on that role.
[Source]
OMG SBVR, EU-Rent case study: "car models are grouped into car groups". Restated at https://kdmanalytics.com/sbvr/EU-Rent.html and https://caminao.blog/community/sample-problems/eu-rent-car/</FIELD><FIELD Name="SyncLink">01A04736-70E4-79E7-AACF-E87A80E92D53</FIELD><FIELD Name="Artificial Key"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Estimated number of Tuples"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Static population"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Namespace"></FIELD><FIELD Name="NamespaceVersion"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Is super type"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Is abstract type">T</FIELD><FIELD Name="OTFT Schema"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Abbreviation"></FIELD><FIELD Name="OTFT Plural"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Temporal"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Transitional"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Concept Type"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Task Status"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Task Color"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Task Background"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Localize Value"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Image URI"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Meta Level">1</FIELD><FIELD Name="Authoritative Synclink">01A04736-70E4-72F5-A774-678A6EEA3AB0</FIELD><FIELD Name="Case Sensitive"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Annotatable"></FIELD><FIELD Name="IsComplexType"></FIELD><FIELD Name="OTFT Article"></FIELD><FIELD Name="IsComposite"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Sensitivity"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Retention Policy"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Created By">claude-code</FIELD><FIELD Name="Created On">20260828 091225.316</FIELD><FIELD Name="Updated By">claude-code</FIELD><FIELD Name="Updated On">20260828 091416.432</FIELD></ROW><ROW><FIELD Name="OTFT Name">R02 Rental Requests Exactly One Car Group</FIELD><FIELD Name="Alias"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Type">R</FIELD><FIELD Name="Derivable?">F</FIELD><FIELD Name="Subtype?">F</FIELD><FIELD Name="Data Type"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Length"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Scale"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Reducable?"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Reduce!"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Comment">[Definition]
It is obligatory that each rental has exactly one requested car group. Enforced structurally: UC + TC on role 1 of "Requested Car Group".
[Source]
OMG SBVR EU-Rent vocabulary and rules (Annex). Summarised at https://kdmanalytics.com/sbvr/EU-Rent.html</FIELD><FIELD Name="SyncLink">01A04736-7381-7676-8838-FC91A0CB1D60</FIELD><FIELD Name="Artificial Key"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Estimated number of Tuples"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Static population"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Namespace"></FIELD><FIELD Name="NamespaceVersion"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Is super type"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Is abstract type">T</FIELD><FIELD Name="OTFT Schema"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Abbreviation"></FIELD><FIELD Name="OTFT Plural"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Temporal"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Transitional"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Concept Type"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Task Status"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Task Color"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Task Background"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Localize Value"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Image URI"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Meta Level">1</FIELD><FIELD Name="Authoritative Synclink">01A04736-7381-7059-92F6-104DCC70C2B7</FIELD><FIELD Name="Case Sensitive"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Annotatable"></FIELD><FIELD Name="IsComplexType"></FIELD><FIELD Name="OTFT Article"></FIELD><FIELD Name="IsComposite"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Sensitivity"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Retention Policy"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Created By">claude-code</FIELD><FIELD Name="Created On">20260828 091225.985</FIELD><FIELD Name="Updated By">claude-code</FIELD><FIELD Name="Updated On">20260828 091419.307</FIELD></ROW><ROW><FIELD Name="OTFT Name">R03 Maximum Three Additional Drivers</FIELD><FIELD Name="Alias"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Type">R</FIELD><FIELD Name="Derivable?">F</FIELD><FIELD Name="Subtype?">F</FIELD><FIELD Name="Data Type"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Length"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Scale"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Reducable?"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Reduce!"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Comment">[Definition]
It is obligatory that each rental has at most three additional drivers. NOT expressible as a uniqueness or totality constraint: it is a cardinality rule over the "Additional Driver" fact type and needs a derivation/constraint expression or application logic.
[Source]
Classic SBVR EU-Rent example rule: "It is obligatory that each rental has at most three additional drivers." See https://kdmanalytics.com/sbvr/sbvr_intro_2.html
[Derivation]
FOR EACH Rental R: COUNT(Additional Driver WHERE Additional Driver.Rental = R) &lt;= 3. A cardinality rule over the M:N fact type "Additional Driver"; it cannot be expressed as a uniqueness constraint, which bounds a count at 1, not at 3. Check on every insert into Additional Driver. Counter-example in the population: rental 10005 with four additional drivers.</FIELD><FIELD Name="SyncLink">01A04736-7647-7E4E-A842-21368E95D343</FIELD><FIELD Name="Artificial Key"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Estimated number of Tuples"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Static population"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Namespace"></FIELD><FIELD Name="NamespaceVersion"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Is super type"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Is abstract type">T</FIELD><FIELD Name="OTFT Schema"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Abbreviation"></FIELD><FIELD Name="OTFT Plural"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Temporal"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Transitional"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Concept Type"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Task Status"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Task Color"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Task Background"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Localize Value"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Image URI"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Meta Level">1</FIELD><FIELD Name="Authoritative Synclink">01A04736-7647-7DE3-9AA5-F135A99DA1AB</FIELD><FIELD Name="Case Sensitive"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Annotatable"></FIELD><FIELD Name="IsComplexType"></FIELD><FIELD Name="OTFT Article"></FIELD><FIELD Name="IsComposite"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Sensitivity"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Retention Policy"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Created By">claude-code</FIELD><FIELD Name="Created On">20260828 091226.695</FIELD><FIELD Name="Updated By">claude-code</FIELD><FIELD Name="Updated On">20260905 172815.960</FIELD></ROW><ROW><FIELD Name="OTFT Name">R04 Barred Driver May Not Drive</FIELD><FIELD Name="Alias"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Type">R</FIELD><FIELD Name="Derivable?">F</FIELD><FIELD Name="Subtype?">F</FIELD><FIELD Name="Data Type"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Length"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Scale"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Reducable?"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Reduce!"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Comment">[Definition]
It is prohibited that a barred driver is the main driver or an additional driver of a rental. A behavioural rule: it can be violated in the real world, which is exactly why EU-Rent records it.
[Source]
EU-Rent business context: "EU-Rent notes bad experiences with drivers and may bar drivers who cause them." https://caminao.blog/community/sample-problems/eu-rent-car/
[Derivation]
FOR EACH Rental R, FOR EACH Driver D IN {Main Driver of Rental[R].Driver} UNION Additional Driver[R].Driver: NOT EXISTS Barred Driver[D]. In other words the population of "Barred Driver" and the union of the two driver roles of a rental must be disjoint. A subset-exclusion constraint between "Barred Driver.Driver" and the driver roles of "Main Driver of Rental" and "Additional Driver" says the same thing declaratively. Counter-example in the population: rental 10004 driven by 1002, who is barred.</FIELD><FIELD Name="SyncLink">01A04736-793B-753F-9BD8-0669D69F4BB3</FIELD><FIELD Name="Artificial Key"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Estimated number of Tuples"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Static population"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Namespace"></FIELD><FIELD Name="NamespaceVersion"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Is super type"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Is abstract type">T</FIELD><FIELD Name="OTFT Schema"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Abbreviation"></FIELD><FIELD Name="OTFT Plural"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Temporal"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Transitional"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Concept Type"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Task Status"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Task Color"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Task Background"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Localize Value"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Image URI"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Meta Level">1</FIELD><FIELD Name="Authoritative Synclink">01A04736-793B-782E-9545-9B376A2A000A</FIELD><FIELD Name="Case Sensitive"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Annotatable"></FIELD><FIELD Name="IsComplexType"></FIELD><FIELD Name="OTFT Article"></FIELD><FIELD Name="IsComposite"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Sensitivity"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Retention Policy"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Created By">claude-code</FIELD><FIELD Name="Created On">20260828 091227.451</FIELD><FIELD Name="Updated By">claude-code</FIELD><FIELD Name="Updated On">20260905 172819.218</FIELD></ROW><ROW><FIELD Name="OTFT Name">R05 Driver Holds Valid Licence</FIELD><FIELD Name="Alias"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Type">R</FIELD><FIELD Name="Derivable?">F</FIELD><FIELD Name="Subtype?">F</FIELD><FIELD Name="Data Type"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Length"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Scale"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Reducable?"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Reduce!"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Comment">[Definition]
It is obligatory that each driver of a rental holds a driving licence whose expiry date is not earlier than the return date of the rental. Partly structural (TC makes licence and expiry mandatory for a Driver); the date comparison is a derivation rule.
[Source]
EU-Rent driver-qualification rules, OMG SBVR EU-Rent case study. https://kdmanalytics.com/sbvr/EU-Rent.html
[Derivation]
FOR EACH Rental R, FOR EACH Driver D IN {Main Driver of Rental[R].Driver} UNION Additional Driver[R].Driver: Licence Expiry[D].Licence Expiry Date &gt;= Rental Period[R].Return Date, and &gt;= Actual Return[R].Actual Return Date once the car is back. Existence of the licence and its expiry date is structural (TC on the Driver roles of "Driving Licence" and "Licence Expiry"); the date comparison is what this derivation adds. Example in the population: driver 1004's licence expires 2026-09-01 while rental 10002 runs until 2026-09-24.</FIELD><FIELD Name="SyncLink">01A04736-7BAF-7FCE-A5EE-AE42991F759B</FIELD><FIELD Name="Artificial Key"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Estimated number of Tuples"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Static population"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Namespace"></FIELD><FIELD Name="NamespaceVersion"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Is super type"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Is abstract type">T</FIELD><FIELD Name="OTFT Schema"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Abbreviation"></FIELD><FIELD Name="OTFT Plural"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Temporal"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Transitional"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Concept Type"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Task Status"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Task Color"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Task Background"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Localize Value"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Image URI"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Meta Level">1</FIELD><FIELD Name="Authoritative Synclink">01A04736-7BAF-7EB8-AFA4-A500C8498E51</FIELD><FIELD Name="Case Sensitive"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Annotatable"></FIELD><FIELD Name="IsComplexType"></FIELD><FIELD Name="OTFT Article"></FIELD><FIELD Name="IsComposite"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Sensitivity"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Retention Policy"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Created By">claude-code</FIELD><FIELD Name="Created On">20260828 091228.079</FIELD><FIELD Name="Updated By">claude-code</FIELD><FIELD Name="Updated On">20260905 172822.533</FIELD></ROW><ROW><FIELD Name="OTFT Name">R06 Minimum Driver Age</FIELD><FIELD Name="Alias"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Type">R</FIELD><FIELD Name="Derivable?">F</FIELD><FIELD Name="Subtype?">F</FIELD><FIELD Name="Data Type"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Length"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Scale"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Reducable?"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Reduce!"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Comment">[Definition]
It is obligatory that each driver of a rental is at least 21 years old on the pick-up date of the rental. Derived from "Date of Birth" and "Rental Period"; not a value constraint, because the comparison is against a moving reference date.
[Source]
EU-Rent driver-qualification rules (SBVR case study). The 21-year threshold matches common European rental practice; see also https://www.autoeurope.com/travel-tips/rental-car-age-requirements/
[Derivation]
FOR EACH Rental R, FOR EACH Driver D IN {Main Driver of Rental[R].Driver} UNION Additional Driver[R].Driver: YEARS_BETWEEN(Date of Birth[D].Birth Date, Rental Period[R].Pick Up Date) &gt;= 21. The threshold 21 is assumed, not sourced (see the open question on the todo list). Example in the population: person 1003, born 2007-02-18, is 19 on any pick-up date in 2026 and may therefore not drive.</FIELD><FIELD Name="SyncLink">01A04736-7F50-7764-A216-9DD667D42103</FIELD><FIELD Name="Artificial Key"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Estimated number of Tuples"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Static population"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Namespace"></FIELD><FIELD Name="NamespaceVersion"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Is super type"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Is abstract type">T</FIELD><FIELD Name="OTFT Schema"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Abbreviation"></FIELD><FIELD Name="OTFT Plural"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Temporal"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Transitional"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Concept Type"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Task Status"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Task Color"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Task Background"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Localize Value"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Image URI"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Meta Level">1</FIELD><FIELD Name="Authoritative Synclink">01A04736-7F50-7333-9254-4D55FF704172</FIELD><FIELD Name="Case Sensitive"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Annotatable"></FIELD><FIELD Name="IsComplexType"></FIELD><FIELD Name="OTFT Article"></FIELD><FIELD Name="IsComposite"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Sensitivity"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Retention Policy"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Created By">claude-code</FIELD><FIELD Name="Created On">20260828 091229.008</FIELD><FIELD Name="Updated By">claude-code</FIELD><FIELD Name="Updated On">20260905 172825.462</FIELD></ROW><ROW><FIELD Name="OTFT Name">R07 Maximum Rental Duration</FIELD><FIELD Name="Alias"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Type">R</FIELD><FIELD Name="Derivable?">F</FIELD><FIELD Name="Subtype?">F</FIELD><FIELD Name="Data Type"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Length"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Scale"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Reducable?"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Reduce!"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Comment">[Definition]
It is obligatory that the rental period of a rental is at most 90 days. A derivation over the two date roles of "Rental Period"; a value constraint on a single label type cannot express it.
[Source]
OMG SBVR EU-Rent case study, rental-duration rules. https://kdmanalytics.com/sbvr/EU-Rent.html
[Derivation]
FOR EACH Rental R: DAYS_BETWEEN(Rental Period[R].Pick Up Date, Rental Period[R].Return Date) &lt;= 90, and Return Date &gt;= Pick Up Date. Both roles live in the one composite fact type "Rental Period", so this is a row-level check on that fact type. The threshold 90 is assumed, not sourced. Counter-example in the population: rental 10006, 2026-09-01 to 2026-12-15, 105 days.</FIELD><FIELD Name="SyncLink">01A04736-8150-7CC1-A8A5-445C7CA23254</FIELD><FIELD Name="Artificial Key"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Estimated number of Tuples"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Static population"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Namespace"></FIELD><FIELD Name="NamespaceVersion"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Is super type"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Is abstract type">T</FIELD><FIELD Name="OTFT Schema"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Abbreviation"></FIELD><FIELD Name="OTFT Plural"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Temporal"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Transitional"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Concept Type"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Task Status"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Task Color"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Task Background"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Localize Value"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Image URI"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Meta Level">1</FIELD><FIELD Name="Authoritative Synclink">01A04736-8150-7BE5-A248-603734EB5300</FIELD><FIELD Name="Case Sensitive"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Annotatable"></FIELD><FIELD Name="IsComplexType"></FIELD><FIELD Name="OTFT Article"></FIELD><FIELD Name="IsComposite"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Sensitivity"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Retention Policy"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Created By">claude-code</FIELD><FIELD Name="Created On">20260828 091229.520</FIELD><FIELD Name="Updated By">claude-code</FIELD><FIELD Name="Updated On">20260905 172828.104</FIELD></ROW><ROW><FIELD Name="OTFT Name">R08 Drop Off Branch Is An EU-Rent Branch</FIELD><FIELD Name="Alias"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Type">R</FIELD><FIELD Name="Derivable?">F</FIELD><FIELD Name="Subtype?">F</FIELD><FIELD Name="Data Type"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Length"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Scale"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Reducable?"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Reduce!"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Comment">[Definition]
It is obligatory that the drop-off branch of a rental is an EU-Rent branch. Enforced structurally: the drop-off role of "Drop Off Branch" is played by Branch, so no other place can be named.
[Source]
SBVR EU-Rent: "a rental incurs a location penalty charge if the drop-off location of the rental is not the EU-Rent site of the return branch of the rental." https://kdmanalytics.com/sbvr/EU-Rent.html</FIELD><FIELD Name="SyncLink">01A04736-8426-7A03-BE03-D24AC5D44010</FIELD><FIELD Name="Artificial Key"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Estimated number of Tuples"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Static population"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Namespace"></FIELD><FIELD Name="NamespaceVersion"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Is super type"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Is abstract type">T</FIELD><FIELD Name="OTFT Schema"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Abbreviation"></FIELD><FIELD Name="OTFT Plural"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Temporal"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Transitional"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Concept Type"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Task Status"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Task Color"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Task Background"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Localize Value"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Image URI"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Meta Level">1</FIELD><FIELD Name="Authoritative Synclink">01A04736-8426-7023-99C5-8B5788F850D6</FIELD><FIELD Name="Case Sensitive"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Annotatable"></FIELD><FIELD Name="IsComplexType"></FIELD><FIELD Name="OTFT Article"></FIELD><FIELD Name="IsComposite"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Sensitivity"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Retention Policy"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Created By">claude-code</FIELD><FIELD Name="Created On">20260828 091230.246</FIELD><FIELD Name="Updated By">claude-code</FIELD><FIELD Name="Updated On">20260828 091440.394</FIELD></ROW><ROW><FIELD Name="OTFT Name">R09 One Way Rental Incurs Location Penalty Charge</FIELD><FIELD Name="Alias"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Type">R</FIELD><FIELD Name="Derivable?">F</FIELD><FIELD Name="Subtype?">F</FIELD><FIELD Name="Data Type"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Length"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Scale"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Reducable?"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Reduce!"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Comment">[Definition]
A rental incurs a location penalty charge if the drop-off branch of the rental is not the pick-up branch of the rental. This is what makes a rental a One-Way Rental. Produces a tuple of "Rental Charge" with charge kind "Location Penalty Charge".
[Source]
SBVR EU-Rent Annex, location-penalty rule; one-way rentals are allowed per the EU-Rent business context. https://caminao.blog/community/sample-problems/eu-rent-car/
[Derivation]
One-Way Rental := Rental R WHERE Pick Up Branch[R].Branch &lt;&gt; Drop Off Branch[R].Branch (the derivation of the subtype). FOR EACH One-Way Rental R: EXISTS Rental Charge[R, 'Location Penalty Charge']. The amount is a business parameter, not derived here. Example in the population: rental 10001, AMS01 to BRU01, carries a Location Penalty Charge of 45.00.</FIELD><FIELD Name="SyncLink">01A04736-8751-7BE9-B042-6C563E1A3646</FIELD><FIELD Name="Artificial Key"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Estimated number of Tuples"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Static population"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Namespace"></FIELD><FIELD Name="NamespaceVersion"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Is super type"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Is abstract type">T</FIELD><FIELD Name="OTFT Schema"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Abbreviation"></FIELD><FIELD Name="OTFT Plural"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Temporal"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Transitional"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Concept Type"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Task Status"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Task Color"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Task Background"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Localize Value"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Image URI"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Meta Level">1</FIELD><FIELD Name="Authoritative Synclink">01A04736-8751-725C-BD37-27744DCCDA50</FIELD><FIELD Name="Case Sensitive"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Annotatable"></FIELD><FIELD Name="IsComplexType"></FIELD><FIELD Name="OTFT Article"></FIELD><FIELD Name="IsComposite"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Sensitivity"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Retention Policy"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Created By">claude-code</FIELD><FIELD Name="Created On">20260828 091231.057</FIELD><FIELD Name="Updated By">claude-code</FIELD><FIELD Name="Updated On">20260905 172830.839</FIELD></ROW><ROW><FIELD Name="OTFT Name">R10 Area Of Usage Rule</FIELD><FIELD Name="Alias"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Type">R</FIELD><FIELD Name="Derivable?">F</FIELD><FIELD Name="Subtype?">F</FIELD><FIELD Name="Data Type"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Length"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Scale"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Reducable?"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Reduce!"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Comment">[Definition]
"No rented car of an open rental may be outside the authorized area of the rental." Grounded in the fact types "Car of Rental", "Rental State" (Open) and "Authorized Area of Rental". A behavioural rule: it CAN be broken, and R11 says what happens then.
[Source]
Verbatim from Ron Ross / Business Rules Journal, "SBVR Speaks on Rules: Violations of Business Rules": https://www.brcommunity.com/articles.php?id=c009 . Motivated by EU-Rent's cross-border insurance concerns.</FIELD><FIELD Name="SyncLink">01A04736-897F-7FDF-BCD7-581DD4883477</FIELD><FIELD Name="Artificial Key"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Estimated number of Tuples"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Static population"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Namespace"></FIELD><FIELD Name="NamespaceVersion"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Is super type"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Is abstract type">T</FIELD><FIELD Name="OTFT Schema"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Abbreviation"></FIELD><FIELD Name="OTFT Plural"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Temporal"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Transitional"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Concept Type"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Task Status"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Task Color"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Task Background"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Localize Value"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Image URI"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Meta Level">1</FIELD><FIELD Name="Authoritative Synclink">01A04736-897F-79E6-A1D0-9A5B88BC54D1</FIELD><FIELD Name="Case Sensitive"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Annotatable"></FIELD><FIELD Name="IsComplexType"></FIELD><FIELD Name="OTFT Article"></FIELD><FIELD Name="IsComposite"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Sensitivity"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Retention Policy"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Created By">claude-code</FIELD><FIELD Name="Created On">20260828 091231.615</FIELD><FIELD Name="Updated By">claude-code</FIELD><FIELD Name="Updated On">20260828 091449.721</FIELD></ROW><ROW><FIELD Name="OTFT Name">R11 Area Of Usage Remedial Rule</FIELD><FIELD Name="Alias"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Type">R</FIELD><FIELD Name="Derivable?">F</FIELD><FIELD Name="Subtype?">F</FIELD><FIELD Name="Data Type"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Length"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Scale"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Reducable?"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Reduce!"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Comment">[Definition]
"An open rental must be canceled if the Area of Usage Rule is violated by the rental." A remedial rule: its trigger is the violation of R10, not a state of the business. Realised as the Open -&gt; Cancelled transition in the Rental Status value constraint.
[Source]
Verbatim from https://www.brcommunity.com/articles.php?id=c009 (Business Rules Journal), which uses it to show the SBVR distinction between a behavioural rule and its remedial response.
[Derivation]
Trigger: FOR EACH Open Rental R (Rental State[R].Rental Status = 'Open') WITH Car of Rental[R]: IF the car is observed in a Local Area L WITH NOT EXISTS Authorized Area of Rental[R, L] THEN R10 is violated and Rental State[R] must move Open -&gt; Cancelled, a transition the "Rental Status" state machine allows. The observation of the car's location is outside the model (no fact type records it), which is why R10 is violable by design and R11 is a remedial rule rather than a constraint.</FIELD><FIELD Name="SyncLink">01A04736-8C61-77BB-B571-E2E46533A6B1</FIELD><FIELD Name="Artificial Key"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Estimated number of Tuples"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Static population"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Namespace"></FIELD><FIELD Name="NamespaceVersion"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Is super type"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Is abstract type">T</FIELD><FIELD Name="OTFT Schema"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Abbreviation"></FIELD><FIELD Name="OTFT Plural"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Temporal"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Transitional"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Concept Type"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Task Status"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Task Color"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Task Background"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Localize Value"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Image URI"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Meta Level">1</FIELD><FIELD Name="Authoritative Synclink">01A04736-8C61-7763-A48C-34FA749AF362</FIELD><FIELD Name="Case Sensitive"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Annotatable"></FIELD><FIELD Name="IsComplexType"></FIELD><FIELD Name="OTFT Article"></FIELD><FIELD Name="IsComposite"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Sensitivity"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Retention Policy"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Created By">claude-code</FIELD><FIELD Name="Created On">20260828 091232.353</FIELD><FIELD Name="Updated By">claude-code</FIELD><FIELD Name="Updated On">20260905 172850.964</FIELD></ROW><ROW><FIELD Name="OTFT Name">R12 Free Upgrade When Requested Group Unavailable</FIELD><FIELD Name="Alias"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Type">R</FIELD><FIELD Name="Derivable?">F</FIELD><FIELD Name="Subtype?">F</FIELD><FIELD Name="Data Type"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Length"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Scale"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Reducable?"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Reduce!"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Comment">[Definition]
If no car of the requested car group is available at the pick-up branch on the pick-up date, EU-Rent must allocate a car of a higher car group, charged at the tariff of the requested car group. The "higher" ordering is the A..F ordering of the Car Group Code value constraint.
[Source]
EU-Rent upgrade policy, a standard element of the case study across its ORM/UML/SBVR retellings. https://kdmanalytics.com/sbvr/EU-Rent.html
[Derivation]
Applies at allocation time. Let G = Requested Car Group[R].Car Group and B = Pick Up Branch[R].Branch. IF NOT EXISTS Car C WITH Home Branch of Car[C].Branch = B AND Car Condition[C].Condition = 'Available' AND Car Group of Car Model[Car Model of Car[C].Car Model].Car Group = G on Rental Period[R].Pick Up Date, THEN allocate a car of a group G' &gt; G (per the Car Group Code order A&lt;B&lt;C&lt;D&lt;E&lt;F) AND the 'Rental Charge' amount = DAYS(Rental Period[R]) x Rental Tariff[G, Country of Local Area[Local Area of Branch[B].Local Area].Country].Daily Rate - the tariff of the REQUESTED group G, not of G'. Availability on a future date needs the reservation inventory, which is out of scope, so this derivation can only be applied on the day of pick-up.</FIELD><FIELD Name="SyncLink">01A04736-8F5C-7EC7-AE68-B18F724DF5FB</FIELD><FIELD Name="Artificial Key"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Estimated number of Tuples"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Static population"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Namespace"></FIELD><FIELD Name="NamespaceVersion"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Is super type"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Is abstract type">T</FIELD><FIELD Name="OTFT Schema"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Abbreviation"></FIELD><FIELD Name="OTFT Plural"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Temporal"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Transitional"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Concept Type"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Task Status"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Task Color"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Task Background"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Localize Value"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Image URI"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Meta Level">1</FIELD><FIELD Name="Authoritative Synclink">01A04736-8F5C-70F2-8C42-1F651741E3DD</FIELD><FIELD Name="Case Sensitive"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Annotatable"></FIELD><FIELD Name="IsComplexType"></FIELD><FIELD Name="OTFT Article"></FIELD><FIELD Name="IsComposite"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Sensitivity"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Retention Policy"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Created By">claude-code</FIELD><FIELD Name="Created On">20260828 091233.116</FIELD><FIELD Name="Updated By">claude-code</FIELD><FIELD Name="Updated On">20260905 172835.400</FIELD></ROW><ROW><FIELD Name="OTFT Name">R13 Allocated Car Matches Or Exceeds Requested Group</FIELD><FIELD Name="Alias"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Type">R</FIELD><FIELD Name="Derivable?">F</FIELD><FIELD Name="Subtype?">F</FIELD><FIELD Name="Data Type"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Length"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Scale"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Reducable?"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Reduce!"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Comment">[Definition]
It is obligatory that the car of a rental is of a car model classified in the requested car group of the rental, or in a higher car group. Joins "Car of Rental" - "Car Model of Car" - "Car Group of Car Model" against "Requested Car Group": a join constraint, not a single-fact-type constraint.
[Source]
Consequence of the EU-Rent upgrade policy; the car-group/car-model/car chain is the standard EU-Rent fleet structure. https://caminao.blog/community/sample-problems/eu-rent-car/
[Derivation]
FOR EACH Rental R WITH Car of Rental[R]: RANK(Car Group of Car Model[Car Model of Car[Car of Rental[R].Car].Car Model].Car Group) &gt;= RANK(Requested Car Group[R].Car Group), where RANK follows the value constraint order of Car Group Code, A&lt;B&lt;C&lt;D&lt;E&lt;F. A join over three fact types, so it cannot be a constraint on any single one. Counter-example in the population: rental 10008 requested group E and was fulfilled with NL-12-ABC-3, a Polo in group A.</FIELD><FIELD Name="SyncLink">01A04736-91C5-728F-B245-54D517AC375F</FIELD><FIELD Name="Artificial Key"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Estimated number of Tuples"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Static population"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Namespace"></FIELD><FIELD Name="NamespaceVersion"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Is super type"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Is abstract type">T</FIELD><FIELD Name="OTFT Schema"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Abbreviation"></FIELD><FIELD Name="OTFT Plural"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Temporal"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Transitional"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Concept Type"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Task Status"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Task Color"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Task Background"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Localize Value"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Image URI"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Meta Level">1</FIELD><FIELD Name="Authoritative Synclink">01A04736-91C5-7677-A933-D9F5BED9C866</FIELD><FIELD Name="Case Sensitive"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Annotatable"></FIELD><FIELD Name="IsComplexType"></FIELD><FIELD Name="OTFT Article"></FIELD><FIELD Name="IsComposite"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Sensitivity"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Retention Policy"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Created By">claude-code</FIELD><FIELD Name="Created On">20260828 091233.732</FIELD><FIELD Name="Updated By">claude-code</FIELD><FIELD Name="Updated On">20260905 172838.282</FIELD></ROW><ROW><FIELD Name="OTFT Name">R14 Service Interval Of 5000 Miles</FIELD><FIELD Name="Alias"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Type">R</FIELD><FIELD Name="Derivable?">F</FIELD><FIELD Name="Subtype?">F</FIELD><FIELD Name="Data Type"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Length"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Scale"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Reducable?"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Reduce!"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Comment">[Definition]
It is obligatory that the odometer reading of a car does not exceed the mileage of its most recent service by more than 5000 miles. Compares "Car Odometer Reading" with the highest "Car Service" mileage for that car.
[Source]
EU-Rent business requirement, quoted verbatim as "Cars are serviced at 5.000 miles intervals" at https://kdmanalytics.com/sbvr/sbvr_intro_2.html
[Derivation]
FOR EACH Car C: Car Odometer Reading[C].Mileage - MAX(Car Service[C].Service Mileage) &lt;= 5000; a car with no Car Service at all is measured from mileage 0. When the difference exceeds 5000 a Scheduled Service is due and the car should move to Condition 'In Service' (Available -&gt; In Service or Rented -&gt; In Service in the Condition state machine). Example in the population: BE-1-XYZ-99 reads 61400 and was last serviced at 55000, 6400 miles ago - overdue, and indeed In Service.</FIELD><FIELD Name="SyncLink">01A04736-94F1-7DAA-ABBE-CA30F0EC8016</FIELD><FIELD Name="Artificial Key"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Estimated number of Tuples"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Static population"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Namespace"></FIELD><FIELD Name="NamespaceVersion"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Is super type"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Is abstract type">T</FIELD><FIELD Name="OTFT Schema"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Abbreviation"></FIELD><FIELD Name="OTFT Plural"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Temporal"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Transitional"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Concept Type"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Task Status"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Task Color"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Task Background"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Localize Value"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Image URI"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Meta Level">1</FIELD><FIELD Name="Authoritative Synclink">01A04736-94F1-7D98-A29D-817C50B541A6</FIELD><FIELD Name="Case Sensitive"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Annotatable"></FIELD><FIELD Name="IsComplexType"></FIELD><FIELD Name="OTFT Article"></FIELD><FIELD Name="IsComposite"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Sensitivity"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Retention Policy"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Created By">claude-code</FIELD><FIELD Name="Created On">20260828 091234.545</FIELD><FIELD Name="Updated By">claude-code</FIELD><FIELD Name="Updated On">20260905 172841.281</FIELD></ROW><ROW><FIELD Name="OTFT Name">R15 Only An Available Car May Be Rented</FIELD><FIELD Name="Alias"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Type">R</FIELD><FIELD Name="Derivable?">F</FIELD><FIELD Name="Subtype?">F</FIELD><FIELD Name="Data Type"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Length"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Scale"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Reducable?"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Reduce!"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Comment">[Definition]
It is prohibited that a car whose condition is "In Service" or "Written Off" is the car of an open rental. The Condition value constraint is a state machine, so the legal transitions already say a car can only go Available -&gt; Rented.
[Source]
Derived from the EU-Rent fleet-management requirements (cars stored at branches, serviced at intervals, withdrawn after damage). https://caminao.blog/community/sample-problems/eu-rent-car/</FIELD><FIELD Name="SyncLink">01A04736-9761-791C-8D73-534E1A56F735</FIELD><FIELD Name="Artificial Key"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Estimated number of Tuples"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Static population"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Namespace"></FIELD><FIELD Name="NamespaceVersion"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Is super type"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Is abstract type">T</FIELD><FIELD Name="OTFT Schema"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Abbreviation"></FIELD><FIELD Name="OTFT Plural"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Temporal"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Transitional"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Concept Type"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Task Status"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Task Color"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Task Background"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Localize Value"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Image URI"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Meta Level">1</FIELD><FIELD Name="Authoritative Synclink">01A04736-9761-7F62-9981-88507CF8C050</FIELD><FIELD Name="Case Sensitive"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Annotatable"></FIELD><FIELD Name="IsComplexType"></FIELD><FIELD Name="OTFT Article"></FIELD><FIELD Name="IsComposite"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Sensitivity"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Retention Policy"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Created By">claude-code</FIELD><FIELD Name="Created On">20260828 091235.169</FIELD><FIELD Name="Updated By">claude-code</FIELD><FIELD Name="Updated On">20260828 091508.760</FIELD></ROW><ROW><FIELD Name="OTFT Name">R16 Rental Is Guaranteed By Credit Card</FIELD><FIELD Name="Alias"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Type">R</FIELD><FIELD Name="Derivable?">F</FIELD><FIELD Name="Subtype?">F</FIELD><FIELD Name="Data Type"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Length"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Scale"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Reducable?"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Reduce!"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Comment">[Definition]
It is obligatory that the renter of a rental has a credit card that guarantees payment. Enforced structurally by the TC on the Customer role of "Customer Credit Card": no customer without a guarantee card.
[Source]
EU-Rent payment and risk-management requirements (unpaid rentals are a recorded bad experience). https://kdmanalytics.com/sbvr/EU-Rent.html</FIELD><FIELD Name="SyncLink">01A04736-9A23-7324-B4C8-8A2483E49FCE</FIELD><FIELD Name="Artificial Key"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Estimated number of Tuples"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Static population"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Namespace"></FIELD><FIELD Name="NamespaceVersion"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Is super type"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Is abstract type">T</FIELD><FIELD Name="OTFT Schema"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Abbreviation"></FIELD><FIELD Name="OTFT Plural"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Temporal"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Transitional"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Concept Type"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Task Status"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Task Color"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Task Background"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Localize Value"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Image URI"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Meta Level">1</FIELD><FIELD Name="Authoritative Synclink">01A04736-9A23-729C-A37B-7027F10D39B8</FIELD><FIELD Name="Case Sensitive"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Annotatable"></FIELD><FIELD Name="IsComplexType"></FIELD><FIELD Name="OTFT Article"></FIELD><FIELD Name="IsComposite"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Sensitivity"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Retention Policy"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Created By">claude-code</FIELD><FIELD Name="Created On">20260828 091235.875</FIELD><FIELD Name="Updated By">claude-code</FIELD><FIELD Name="Updated On">20260828 091512.208</FIELD></ROW><ROW><FIELD Name="OTFT Name">R17 One Tariff Per Car Group Per Country</FIELD><FIELD Name="Alias"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Type">R</FIELD><FIELD Name="Derivable?">F</FIELD><FIELD Name="Subtype?">F</FIELD><FIELD Name="Data Type"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Length"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Scale"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Reducable?"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Reduce!"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Comment">[Definition]
It is necessary that all cars in a car group have the same rental tariff within a country. Enforced structurally: the tariff hangs off Car Group, never off Car or Car Model, and the UC over (Car Group, Country) admits exactly one daily rate.
[Source]
Verbatim EU-Rent requirement: "all cars in a car group have the same rental tariff". https://caminao.blog/community/sample-problems/eu-rent-car/ and https://kdmanalytics.com/sbvr/sbvr_intro_2.html</FIELD><FIELD Name="SyncLink">01A04736-9CF6-7688-A02B-2DEB4B37A870</FIELD><FIELD Name="Artificial Key"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Estimated number of Tuples"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Static population"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Namespace"></FIELD><FIELD Name="NamespaceVersion"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Is super type"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Is abstract type">T</FIELD><FIELD Name="OTFT Schema"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Abbreviation"></FIELD><FIELD Name="OTFT Plural"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Temporal"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Transitional"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Concept Type"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Task Status"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Task Color"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Task Background"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Localize Value"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Image URI"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Meta Level">1</FIELD><FIELD Name="Authoritative Synclink">01A04736-9CF6-7A49-A1DC-14DE74FA1C14</FIELD><FIELD Name="Case Sensitive"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Annotatable"></FIELD><FIELD Name="IsComplexType"></FIELD><FIELD Name="OTFT Article"></FIELD><FIELD Name="IsComposite"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Sensitivity"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Retention Policy"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Created By">claude-code</FIELD><FIELD Name="Created On">20260828 091236.598</FIELD><FIELD Name="Updated By">claude-code</FIELD><FIELD Name="Updated On">20260828 091515.826</FIELD></ROW><ROW><FIELD Name="OTFT Name">R18 Late Return Incurs Penalty</FIELD><FIELD Name="Alias"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Type">R</FIELD><FIELD Name="Derivable?">F</FIELD><FIELD Name="Subtype?">F</FIELD><FIELD Name="Data Type"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Length"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Scale"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Reducable?"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Reduce!"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Comment">[Definition]
A rental incurs a late return penalty if the actual return date of the rental is later than its agreed return date. Compares "Actual Return" with "Rental Period"; also raises a bad experience of kind "Late Return".
[Source]
EU-Rent: customers "may become blacklisted due to delayed car returns or unpaid rentals" - the ORM retelling of the case. See the EU-Rent overview in ORM literature and https://kdmanalytics.com/sbvr/EU-Rent.html
[Derivation]
FOR EACH Rental R WITH Actual Return[R]: IF Actual Return[R].Actual Return Date &gt; Rental Period[R].Return Date THEN EXISTS Rental Charge[R, 'Late Return Penalty'] WITH Charge Amount = DAYS_BETWEEN(Rental Period[R].Return Date, Actual Return[R].Actual Return Date) x the daily rate of the rental (the tariff lookup of R12). The per-day rate of the penalty is assumed to equal the daily rate. Example in the population: rental 10003 was due 2026-08-08 and returned 2026-08-11, three days late, and carries a Late Return Penalty of 90.00.</FIELD><FIELD Name="SyncLink">01A04736-9FA6-7417-8CC2-869F3CD24C3E</FIELD><FIELD Name="Artificial Key"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Estimated number of Tuples"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Static population"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Namespace"></FIELD><FIELD Name="NamespaceVersion"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Is super type"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Is abstract type">T</FIELD><FIELD Name="OTFT Schema"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Abbreviation"></FIELD><FIELD Name="OTFT Plural"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Temporal"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Transitional"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Concept Type"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Task Status"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Task Color"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Task Background"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Localize Value"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Image URI"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Meta Level">1</FIELD><FIELD Name="Authoritative Synclink">01A04736-9FA6-74C1-8268-3FFFFB7F83F2</FIELD><FIELD Name="Case Sensitive"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Annotatable"></FIELD><FIELD Name="IsComplexType"></FIELD><FIELD Name="OTFT Article"></FIELD><FIELD Name="IsComposite"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Sensitivity"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Retention Policy"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Created By">claude-code</FIELD><FIELD Name="Created On">20260828 091237.286</FIELD><FIELD Name="Updated By">claude-code</FIELD><FIELD Name="Updated On">20260905 172844.529</FIELD></ROW><ROW><FIELD Name="OTFT Name">R19 Three Bad Experiences Bar A Driver</FIELD><FIELD Name="Alias"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Type">R</FIELD><FIELD Name="Derivable?">F</FIELD><FIELD Name="Subtype?">F</FIELD><FIELD Name="Data Type"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Length"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Scale"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Reducable?"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Reduce!"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Comment">[Definition]
A driver must be barred from renting if the driver has caused three or more bad experiences. Counts tuples of "Bad Experience" per driver and asserts "Barred Driver". The threshold is EU-Rent policy, so it is a rule and not a structural constraint.
[Source]
EU-Rent: "the company tracks bad experiences with drivers, including police actions, unpaid fines, vehicle damage, and non-return incidents" and has "authority to bar problematic drivers". https://caminao.blog/community/sample-problems/eu-rent-car/
[Derivation]
FOR EACH Driver D: IF COUNT(Bad Experience WHERE Bad Experience.Driver = D) &gt;= 3 THEN Barred Driver[D]. "Barred Driver" is kept as an asserted (not derivable) fact type on purpose: the sources say EU-Rent MAY bar a driver, so the count triggers a decision rather than deriving it. The threshold 3, and whether it is lifetime or per period, are open questions on the todo list. Example in the population: driver 1002 has three bad experiences (Late Return, Unpaid Fine, Damage To Car) and is barred.</FIELD><FIELD Name="SyncLink">01A04736-A28F-782B-8066-B2715DCA5A9A</FIELD><FIELD Name="Artificial Key"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Estimated number of Tuples"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Static population"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Namespace"></FIELD><FIELD Name="NamespaceVersion"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Is super type"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Is abstract type">T</FIELD><FIELD Name="OTFT Schema"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Abbreviation"></FIELD><FIELD Name="OTFT Plural"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Temporal"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Transitional"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Concept Type"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Task Status"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Task Color"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Task Background"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Localize Value"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Image URI"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Meta Level">1</FIELD><FIELD Name="Authoritative Synclink">01A04736-A28F-7020-A363-ADCF28FE2C1F</FIELD><FIELD Name="Case Sensitive"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Annotatable"></FIELD><FIELD Name="IsComplexType"></FIELD><FIELD Name="OTFT Article"></FIELD><FIELD Name="IsComposite"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Sensitivity"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Retention Policy"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Created By">claude-code</FIELD><FIELD Name="Created On">20260828 091238.029</FIELD><FIELD Name="Updated By">claude-code</FIELD><FIELD Name="Updated On">20260905 172847.714</FIELD></ROW><ROW><FIELD Name="OTFT Name">R20 Renter Drives Or Nominates A Driver</FIELD><FIELD Name="Alias"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Type">R</FIELD><FIELD Name="Derivable?">F</FIELD><FIELD Name="Subtype?">F</FIELD><FIELD Name="Data Type"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Length"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Scale"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Reducable?"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Reduce!"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Comment">[Definition]
It is obligatory that the main driver of a rental is the renter of that rental, or that the renter has nominated the main driver. A renter need not drive (a company may rent), but somebody qualified must - hence Main Driver of Rental is mandatory for a Rental.
[Source]
EU-Rent: "each rented car has one or more registered drivers"; renter and driver are separate roles of a person in the EU-Rent vocabulary. ORM retelling of EU-Rent; https://kdmanalytics.com/sbvr/EU-Rent.html</FIELD><FIELD Name="SyncLink">01A04736-A3B2-7B4D-8D4F-8D6CC18A92DB</FIELD><FIELD Name="Artificial Key"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Estimated number of Tuples"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Static population"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Namespace"></FIELD><FIELD Name="NamespaceVersion"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Is super type"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Is abstract type">T</FIELD><FIELD Name="OTFT Schema"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Abbreviation"></FIELD><FIELD Name="OTFT Plural"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Temporal"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Transitional"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Concept Type"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Task Status"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Task Color"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Task Background"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Localize Value"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Image URI"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Meta Level">1</FIELD><FIELD Name="Authoritative Synclink">01A04736-A3B2-75B6-8D25-80CEB4FA8E85</FIELD><FIELD Name="Case Sensitive"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Annotatable"></FIELD><FIELD Name="IsComplexType"></FIELD><FIELD Name="OTFT Article"></FIELD><FIELD Name="IsComposite"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Sensitivity"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Retention Policy"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Created By">claude-code</FIELD><FIELD Name="Created On">20260828 091238.322</FIELD><FIELD Name="Updated By">claude-code</FIELD><FIELD Name="Updated On">20260828 091527.106</FIELD></ROW><ROW><FIELD Name="OTFT Name">R22 One Car On Rental At A Time</FIELD><FIELD Name="Alias"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Type">R</FIELD><FIELD Name="Derivable?">F</FIELD><FIELD Name="Subtype?">F</FIELD><FIELD Name="Data Type"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Length"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Scale"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Reducable?"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Reduce!"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Comment">[Definition]
It is obligatory that a customer has at most one open rental at a time. A customer may hold any number of reservations (rentals in state Requested), but only one car may be out on rental against that customer. A behavioural rule: it is checked at pick-up, when a rental moves Requested -&gt; Open or a walk-in rental is opened, and it is a cardinality rule over Open Rental joined with "Renter of Rental" - not a uniqueness constraint, because Renter of Rental legitimately holds several rentals per customer over time.
[Source]
Verbatim from the original case study: "A customer can have several reservations but only one car rented at a time." - Appendix D "Case Study: EU-Rent Car Rentals" (Model Systems Ltd.) of the Business Rules Group / GUIDE Business Rules Project final report "Defining Business Rules ~ What Are They Really?" (1995; rev. 1.3 July 2000), section Customers. https://www.businessrulesgroup.org/first_paper/BRG-whatisBR_3ed.pdf
[Derivation]
FOR EACH Customer C: COUNT(Open Rental R WHERE Renter of Rental[R].Customer = C) &lt;= 1, where Open Rental := Rental R WHERE Rental State[R].Rental Status = 'Open'. Check when a rental of C is about to enter state Open: refuse the transition if another Open Rental of C exists. Reservations are not limited: COUNT(Rental R WHERE Renter of Rental[R].Customer = C AND Rental State[R].Rental Status = 'Requested') is unbounded. Counter-example in the population: rental 10009, renter 1001, in state Open while rental 10001 of the same customer is still Open.</FIELD><FIELD Name="SyncLink">01A07CB5-9E7F-70B7-969D-422961FECB49</FIELD><FIELD Name="Artificial Key"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Estimated number of Tuples"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Static population"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Namespace"></FIELD><FIELD Name="NamespaceVersion"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Is super type"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Is abstract type">T</FIELD><FIELD Name="OTFT Schema"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Abbreviation"></FIELD><FIELD Name="OTFT Plural"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Temporal"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Transitional"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Concept Type"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Task Status"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Task Color"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Task Background"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Localize Value"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Image URI"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Meta Level">1</FIELD><FIELD Name="Authoritative Synclink"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Case Sensitive"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Annotatable"></FIELD><FIELD Name="IsComplexType"></FIELD><FIELD Name="OTFT Article"></FIELD><FIELD Name="IsComposite"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Sensitivity"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Retention Policy"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Created By">mcp-agent</FIELD><FIELD Name="Created On">20260907 183112.511</FIELD><FIELD Name="Updated By">mcp-agent</FIELD><FIELD Name="Updated On">20260907 183130.803</FIELD></ROW><ROW><FIELD Name="OTFT Name">R23 Signing Driver Has No Car On Rental</FIELD><FIELD Name="Alias"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Type">R</FIELD><FIELD Name="Derivable?">F</FIELD><FIELD Name="Subtype?">F</FIELD><FIELD Name="Data Type"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Length"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Scale"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Reducable?"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Reduce!"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Comment">[Definition]
It is prohibited that the driver who signs the rental agreement of a rental currently has an EU-Rent car on rental. In this model Rental IS the rental agreement (see the concept Rental Agreement) and the signing driver is the main driver of the rental (R20: the renter drives, or nominates a driver), so the rule reads: at pick-up, the main driver of the rental must not be the main driver of any other open rental. It complements R22, which limits the customer; R23 limits the person behind the wheel, who may be driving on someone else's contract.
[Source]
Verbatim from the original case study: "The driver who signs the rental agreement must not currently have a EU-Rent car on rental." - Appendix D "Case Study: EU-Rent Car Rentals" (Model Systems Ltd.) of the Business Rules Group / GUIDE Business Rules Project final report "Defining Business Rules ~ What Are They Really?" (1995; rev. 1.3 July 2000), section EU-Rent Business Rules, rental pick-up. https://www.businessrulesgroup.org/first_paper/BRG-whatisBR_3ed.pdf
[Derivation]
At the moment Rental R enters state Open: NOT EXISTS Open Rental R2 WITH R2 &lt;&gt; R AND Main Driver of Rental[R2].Driver = Main Driver of Rental[R].Driver, where Open Rental := Rental R WHERE Rental State[R].Rental Status = 'Open'. Equivalently, at any time: FOR EACH Driver D: COUNT(Open Rental R WHERE Main Driver of Rental[R].Driver = D) &lt;= 1. Additional drivers are not restricted by this rule. Counter-example in the population: rental 10010, main driver 1001, in state Open while rental 10001, which 1001 also drives, is still Open.</FIELD><FIELD Name="SyncLink">01A07CB5-A185-7235-A900-08FD54007EF1</FIELD><FIELD Name="Artificial Key"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Estimated number of Tuples"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Static population"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Namespace"></FIELD><FIELD Name="NamespaceVersion"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Is super type"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Is abstract type">T</FIELD><FIELD Name="OTFT Schema"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Abbreviation"></FIELD><FIELD Name="OTFT Plural"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Temporal"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Transitional"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Concept Type"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Task Status"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Task Color"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Task Background"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Localize Value"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Image URI"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Meta Level">1</FIELD><FIELD Name="Authoritative Synclink"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Case Sensitive"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Annotatable"></FIELD><FIELD Name="IsComplexType"></FIELD><FIELD Name="OTFT Article"></FIELD><FIELD Name="IsComposite"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Sensitivity"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Retention Policy"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Created By">mcp-agent</FIELD><FIELD Name="Created On">20260907 183113.285</FIELD><FIELD Name="Updated By">mcp-agent</FIELD><FIELD Name="Updated On">20260907 183139.804</FIELD></ROW><ROW><FIELD Name="OTFT Name">Registration Number</FIELD><FIELD Name="Alias"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Type">L</FIELD><FIELD Name="Derivable?"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Subtype?">F</FIELD><FIELD Name="Data Type">string</FIELD><FIELD Name="Length"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Scale"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Reducable?"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Reduce!"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Comment"></FIELD><FIELD Name="SyncLink">01A04731-BD3D-7BB6-998F-FEB219EBE5C6</FIELD><FIELD Name="Artificial Key"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Estimated number of Tuples"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Static population"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Namespace"></FIELD><FIELD Name="NamespaceVersion"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Is super type"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Is abstract type"></FIELD><FIELD Name="OTFT Schema"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Abbreviation"></FIELD><FIELD Name="OTFT Plural"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Temporal"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Transitional"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Concept Type"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Task Status"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Task Color"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Task Background"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Localize Value"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Image URI"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Meta Level">1</FIELD><FIELD Name="Authoritative Synclink">01A04731-BD3D-74DA-8037-F5831CA92BF7</FIELD><FIELD Name="Case Sensitive"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Annotatable"></FIELD><FIELD Name="IsComplexType"></FIELD><FIELD Name="OTFT Article"></FIELD><FIELD Name="IsComposite"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Sensitivity"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Retention Policy"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Created By">claude-code</FIELD><FIELD Name="Created On">20260828 090717.181</FIELD><FIELD Name="Updated By"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Updated On"></FIELD></ROW><ROW><FIELD Name="OTFT Name">Rental</FIELD><FIELD Name="Alias"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Type">N</FIELD><FIELD Name="Derivable?">F</FIELD><FIELD Name="Subtype?">F</FIELD><FIELD Name="Data Type"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Length"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Scale"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Reducable?"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Reduce!"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Comment">[Definition]
An agreement under which EU-Rent provides a car of a requested car group to a customer for a period, from a pick-up branch to a drop-off branch. The central object type of the model: nearly every business rule is about a rental.
[Example]
Rental 10001: contracted by customer 1001, group B requested, picked up at AMS01 on 2026-09-01, dropped off at BRU01 on 2026-09-05, fulfilled with NL-34-DEF-5. One-way, so it incurs a location penalty charge.
[Source]
EU-Rent case study, OMG SBVR Annex. Overviews: https://kdmanalytics.com/sbvr/EU-Rent.html , https://caminao.blog/community/sample-problems/eu-rent-car/ . EU-Rent was originally developed by Model Systems Ltd. and popularised by the Business Rules Group.</FIELD><FIELD Name="SyncLink">01A04732-0C75-70DA-8AE4-2876EFA701D6</FIELD><FIELD Name="Artificial Key"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Estimated number of Tuples"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Static population">F</FIELD><FIELD Name="Namespace"></FIELD><FIELD Name="NamespaceVersion"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Is super type">T</FIELD><FIELD Name="Is abstract type"></FIELD><FIELD Name="OTFT Schema"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Abbreviation"></FIELD><FIELD Name="OTFT Plural"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Temporal"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Transitional"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Concept Type"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Task Status"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Task Color"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Task Background"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Localize Value"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Image URI"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Meta Level">1</FIELD><FIELD Name="Authoritative Synclink">01A04732-0C75-76BE-B17E-00AECA329F60</FIELD><FIELD Name="Case Sensitive"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Annotatable"></FIELD><FIELD Name="IsComplexType"></FIELD><FIELD Name="OTFT Article"></FIELD><FIELD Name="IsComposite"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Sensitivity"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Retention Policy"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Created By">claude-code</FIELD><FIELD Name="Created On">20260828 090737.461</FIELD><FIELD Name="Updated By">claude-code</FIELD><FIELD Name="Updated On">20260828 091824.264</FIELD></ROW><ROW><FIELD Name="OTFT Name">Rental Agreement</FIELD><FIELD Name="Alias"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Type">C</FIELD><FIELD Name="Derivable?">F</FIELD><FIELD Name="Subtype?">F</FIELD><FIELD Name="Data Type"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Length"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Scale"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Reducable?"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Reduce!"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Comment">[Definition]
The signed contract that records a rental. In this model the agreement is not a separate object type: Rental IS the agreement. Kept as a glossary concept because the business says "rental agreement" where the model says "rental".</FIELD><FIELD Name="SyncLink">01A07226-EE36-707F-91D1-CB35EEA8E4EF</FIELD><FIELD Name="Artificial Key"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Estimated number of Tuples"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Static population"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Namespace"></FIELD><FIELD Name="NamespaceVersion"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Is super type"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Is abstract type">T</FIELD><FIELD Name="OTFT Schema"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Abbreviation"></FIELD><FIELD Name="OTFT Plural"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Temporal"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Transitional"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Concept Type"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Task Status"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Task Color"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Task Background"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Localize Value"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Image URI"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Meta Level">1</FIELD><FIELD Name="Authoritative Synclink"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Case Sensitive"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Annotatable"></FIELD><FIELD Name="IsComplexType"></FIELD><FIELD Name="OTFT Article"></FIELD><FIELD Name="IsComposite"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Sensitivity"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Retention Policy"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Created By">claude-code</FIELD><FIELD Name="Created On">20260905 171909.110</FIELD><FIELD Name="Updated By">claude-code</FIELD><FIELD Name="Updated On">20260905 171930.339</FIELD></ROW><ROW><FIELD Name="OTFT Name">Rental Charge</FIELD><FIELD Name="Alias"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Type">F</FIELD><FIELD Name="Derivable?">F</FIELD><FIELD Name="Subtype?">F</FIELD><FIELD Name="Data Type"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Length"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Scale"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Reducable?"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Reduce!"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Comment"></FIELD><FIELD Name="SyncLink">01A04732-1908-7894-A434-694D7301BA31</FIELD><FIELD Name="Artificial Key"></FIELD><FIELD Name="Estimated number of Tuples"></FIELD><FIELD Name=